  "design": {
    "prototype": "critique",
    "critique": {
      "preserve": [
        "The Gum-Gum Pistol remains a clear elastic ranged-punch identity, consistent with Luffy's signature attack.",
        "The three paths have distinct identities: elastic coverage/control, Haki utility/control, and Gear-based burst progression.",
        "The Gear Five form is correctly represented as an encounter configuration rather than an unsupported runtime transformation."
      ],
      "findings": [
        {
          "priority": 1,
          "candidatePaths": [
            "/actions/4",
            "/actions/4/targeting/type",
            "/actions/4/delivery/maximumTargetsPerProjectile"
          ],
          "sourceClaimIndices": [23, 24],
          "observation": "The reported schema failure is localized to the Gear Five action. Its targeting uses type \"area\", although targeting must select enemies directly and area is a delivery shape. The same area delivery also carries the projectile-specific maximumTargetsPerProjectile field, leaving the area schema branch unmatched.",
          "revision": "Use a supported enemy-priority targeting type such as \"first\" or \"strongest\", retain delivery.type \"area\" and radiusWorldUnits, and remove the projectile-specific cap in favor of the area branch's supported target cap. Re-run output-schema validation."
        },
        {
          "priority": 2,
          "candidatePaths": [
            "/resources/0",
            "/resources/0/generation/0",
            "/actions/0",
            "/upgradeGraph/nodes/10"
          ],
          "sourceClaimIndices": [16, 17],
          "observation": "Stamina is unavailable by default, but the base primary action is already configured to generate stamina on hit. Unless enable-resource implicitly gates that generation, the base build references an unavailable resource before Gear Escalation tier 1 grants it.",
          "revision": "Make the stamina-generation dependency explicitly activate with gear-escalation-1 using supported resource operations, or otherwise ensure the disabled resource is not referenced by the base action. Keep the finite cap and recovery."
        },
        {
          "priority": 3,
          "candidatePaths": ["/upgradeGraph/nodes/6", "/actions/0/effects"],
          "sourceClaimIndices": [30, 32],
          "observation": "The node named Future Sight only increases reveal duration from 2.5 to 4 seconds. Reveal represents detection, but the supplied evidence describes Future Sight as seeing several seconds into the future; the current mechanic does not alter prediction, target ordering, or avoidance.",
          "revision": "Either rename and describe this as extended Observation Haki, or implement a supported targeting/reveal change that materially represents predictive awareness. Do not present duration-only reveal as literal Future Sight."
        },
        {
          "priority": 3,
          "candidatePaths": ["/upgradeGraph/nodes/7", "/statuses/0", "/actions/0/targeting"],
          "sourceClaimIndices": [31],
          "observation": "Conqueror's Stagger is applied to every primary-hit target because targeting is unrestricted and the status has no eligibility condition. The source claim limits Conqueror's Haki incapacitation to weak-willed people or animals near Luffy.",
          "revision": "Use supplied game-context status resistance or eligibility to restrict the stagger where appropriate. If that context is unavailable, describe the effect as a generalized pressure adaptation rather than an unrestricted Conqueror's Haki knockout effect."
        }
      ],
      "uncertainties": [
        "The draft failed unchanged schema validation, so reference integrity, numeric-bound checks, legal-selection checks, and lifecycle compilation were not completed.",
        "No combat simulation or balance evidence is available; cadence, stamina economy, control uptime, and Gear Five performance remain unverified.",
